notes={'docs/formal/BOUNDED_NUMERIC_PROFILE.md': 'Accepted numeric/exact-1 is bounded to reachable operators in rules/campaign2-bounded-bridge/0.1-candidate, not a universal psychological numeric law. RulesVersion requires but cannot synthesize independently committed NumericProfileVersion. Arbitrary-precision integer and reduced rational arithmetic; negative floor differs from truncation; checked time bounds and remainder propagation do not clamp. Fixed OBS pulse yields [1,1] without rescaling and five Always ADAPT gates use g=1 without scale division. Semantic Number/coercion forbidden, representation dispatch/bytes allowed. Build-supported RoundEven/CeilDiv, dice, conversion, saturation and general quantization are not automatically admitted operations. Zero draws retain independent RNG version field. Header and named source tests are historical evidence pointers, not fresh conformance or newer numeric-profile coverage.', 'docs/formal/EVENT_ORDERING.md': 'Accepted ordering/0.2 and phase registry2 preserve lexicographic DueAt/Phase/run-global EventSequence; opaque gaps and phase150 settlement sentinel are not domain events or durations. Same/later phase scheduling allowed with later sequence; earlier-phase backedge fails. Same-instant reads see earlier staged state but external publication/saves only settled committed state. Any failure discards whole-instant patches/events/trace and restores allocators then terminal Failed; diagnostic is non-authoritative, no retry or drop-and-continue. Strict lane-entry cutoff prevents truth at10/120 reopening that lane. Phase52 body effect cannot feed current50; temporal availability alone grants no ReadDomain or ORD001 resolution. Saved queue, IDs, analytical remainders, coupling input and per-observer perception allocators are preserved without reminting; run-global sequence distinct from observer identity. Ceiling changes model parameter identity and never postpones remaining work. Historical ORD003/004 candidate labels read with concluding applicable-vector acceptance/reopen rule, not blanket future seam closure. ORD001/002/005 general obligations remain scoped; source claims no new current-owner blocker or fresh replay.', 'docs/formal/STATE_MODEL.md': 'Accepted state/0.2 substrate enforcement is distinct from historical proposed/unresolved psychological owner rows and later scoped seam qualification. Exactly one registered owner per leaf, one owner may own multiple leaves; ownership registry and value/removal grammar are committed model identity, not initialization or producer identity. Observer continuant/event files and allocators represent fallible perception, not truth identity; no retroactive truth repair or semantic ordinal magnitude. Capability-limited typed reads record actual concrete dependencies separately from possible reads; derived input must declare source/transformation. WRT validates path structurally before registration/read checks, then declared leaf, owner and operation semantics before emitted events/output dependencies. Earliest overlap INVALID_PATH does not erase independent OWNERSHIP_OVERLAP; diagnosis must identify malformed construct, with truth leak more specific. Canonical patches reject duplicate/ancestor overlap, aliases and stale preconditions; hash equality alone never authorizes writes or proves structural equality. Cognitive evidence and automatic truth-side regulatory/procedural adaptation remain distinct typed routes; no implicit conversion. SEMG applicability is consumer-relative, not a global confidence/visibility field; SEMH reservation only survives with immutable14/124 envelope and separate companions. Frozen pre-attempt expectation cannot be reconstructed after learning. Historical allocation-pending/shape-only notes do not deny later bounded registration, and acceptance does not supply missing psychological contracts.', 'docs/formal/SEAM_CONTRACT_TEMPLATE.md': 'Normative authoring template requires all headings or explicit reasoned not-applicable; it is not an instantiated seam, executable schema or passed experiment. Acceptance requires zero unresolved decision affecting authoritative output, writes, ordering, random result, epistemic boundary, invariant or verdict. Required phenomena, exact transforms, read/write capabilities, rollback, numeric points, comparators, proof, exclusions and reopen conditions must be explicit. Tests establish conformance to specified semantics and cannot invent missing semantics. Template acceptance criterion does not erase explicitly excluded future research scope or elevate local bounded representation choices into owner rulings.'}
